!!! 11-books.matrix
!!! Books (Ny modules), libraries, linking, visibility and book globals.
!!!
!!! Book-level initialisers run in declaration order, not lexical name order.
!!! A typed forward reference type-checks and still fails at runtime if it
!!! reads before initialisation; Matrix does not invent a zero. Arbitrary
!!! top-level statements are not an initialisation mechanism.
!!!
!!! This file pairs with 11-books-pricing.matrix.

book tour.billing

!!! Every read form. The path is the book name, not a file path.
read ny.lang.io.file
read ny.lang.core
read subtotal, volume_discount from tour.pricing
read ny.lang.collections as collections
read everything from ny.lang.math

!!! Book globals belong to their declared book and have "book::name" storage
!!! identity in NIL. Two books may declare the same name without sharing
!!! storage. Aggregate globals remain interpreter-only.
public variable audit_level as number is 1
value internal_seed as number is 40

!!! An initialiser may read an earlier one in the same book.
value derived_seed as number is internal_seed plus 2

!!! A re-export. Consumers of tour.billing see these names.
cite subtotal, volume_discount from tour.pricing

!!! Private to this book: no "public" modifier.
!!! Scalar-to-text conversion is an interpreted-route capability. Native
!!! ordinary casts reject it explicitly rather than supplying an alternative
!!! conversion, so this function is interpreted-only.
format_cents receives cents as number returns text begin paragraph
    give cents becomes text
end paragraph

public net_total receives unit_price as number, quantity as number returns number begin paragraph
    !!! Names linked selectively are called unqualified.
    value gross    is subtotal with unit_price being unit_price, quantity being quantity
    value discount is volume_discount with amount being gross, quantity being quantity
    give gross minus discount
end paragraph

main returns number begin paragraph

    !!! A qualified reference uses "::", which is kept rather than
    !!! naturalised: a NIL storage identity is exactly "book::name", and
    !!! cross-language identity is the point of the exercise.
    set tour.billing::audit_level to 3
    say tour.billing::audit_level
    say derived_seed

    say "MODULAR BILLING"
    say net_total with unit_price being 17, quantity being 12
    say format_cents with cents being 1799

    give 0
end paragraph
